# PR Description File (Issue-Based)

## When to create

When opening or preparing a pull request for **Issue N**, always add a PR description file so reviewers and automation have a clear summary.

## File naming and location

- **Path:** `docs/GITHUB/PR/M<MS>/PR_<N>_DESCRIPTION.md`
- **N:** GitHub issue number the PR closes (e.g. 1, 2, 12).
- **MS:** milestone number — folder **`M<MS>`** matches the issue doc folder under `docs/GITHUB/ISSUES/M<MS>/`.

**Examples**

- Issue 1 (M1) → `docs/GITHUB/PR/M1/PR_1_DESCRIPTION.md`
- Issue 5 (M2) → `docs/GITHUB/PR/M2/PR_5_DESCRIPTION.md`

**A second PR against an issue that is already closed** — a fix, or the bookkeeping that can only run
after the merge — is a **follow-up**: `docs/GITHUB/PR/M<MS>/PR_<N>_FOLLOWUP_DESCRIPTION.md`
(e.g. `docs/GITHUB/PR/M1/PR_7_FOLLOWUP_DESCRIPTION.md`). It keeps the same `Issue/<N>/<slug>` branch
and `Issue <N>: ` commit prefix.

## Required content

1. **Title / summary** — Short description of what the PR does (can match the issue title).
2. **Milestone link** — Link to the GitHub milestone when applicable.
3. **Closing line** — Explicitly state that the PR closes the issue, using one of:
   - `Closes #N`
   - `Fixes #N`

Place the closing line at the end of the file (or in a "Closes" section) so the issue is auto-closed when the PR is merged.

**A follow-up ends `Refs #N` instead**, because the issue is already closed and there is nothing left
to close — say what closed it: `Refs #7 (already closed by #116; this PR closes nothing new)`.
`scripts/check_pr_conventions.py` accepts either form and will fail the PR if neither is present.

## Forbidden content

The description must **not** contain the generator line

```text
🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)
```

or any equivalent "generated with / generated by <assistant>" footer, in the file or in the PR body
posted to GitHub. `Closes #N` is the last line.

**Check before opening the PR**

```bash
grep -rn "Generated with" docs/GITHUB/PR/ && echo "remove the generator line"
```

## Example

**File:** `docs/GITHUB/PR/M1/PR_1_DESCRIPTION.md`

```markdown
# PR: Docker + Postgres (Issue 1)

Adds Docker-based run environment: Dockerfile, docker-compose, app on port 8000, and README instructions for `docker-compose up`, `/health`, and `/docs`.

Closes #1
```

## Workflow

1. Finish work on branch `Issue/N/short-slug`.
2. Add or update `docs/GITHUB/PR/M<MS>/PR_<N>_DESCRIPTION.md` with the summary and closing line.
3. Push and open the PR; paste or reference the description so the PR body contains "Closes #N".
